<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="112" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Implement C1.4 L2 Dataverse registry client (MI-native, DefaultAzureCredential)</title>
    <phase>C'' Wave G-1 -- Foundation</phase>
    <gate>blocked</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>New greenfield client consumed by H0.5 (re-consent semantics), H13 (Ready writer), and the I5 guard -- correctness-critical registry read/write path. FULL per l2-controlplane + auth tags.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>High-blast-radius per parent task instructions (L2 control-plane scaffold class) -- feeds three downstream correctness-critical consumers; Opus tier.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>111</deps>
    <tags>l2-controlplane, auth, path-x, dataverse</tags>
    <estimated-effort>6-9 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Implement the C1.4 L2 Dataverse registry client in Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Registry/: an interface (IDataverseEnvironmentRegistryClient, replacing the placeholder NullDataverseEnvironmentRegistryClient) + a raw-HttpClient + DefaultAzureCredential(ManagedIdentityClientId) implementation targeting {adminEnvUrl}/.default scope, matching the idiom DataverseWebApiHealthProbe already uses. Methods: read a registry row by customerId/tenantId, and (for task 184's consumption) PATCH sprk_setupstatus + related fields by GUID. This client is MI-native from day one -- built once, consumed by H0.5's registry swap (task 122), H13's Ready writer (task 184), and the I5 concurrency guard's Dataverse-backed store if that guard is later re-pointed off its interim BFF-app-reg secret credential (out of THIS task's scope, note only).</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in raw HttpClient + DefaultAzureCredential Dataverse Web API clients (the H7/H10/H11/H12c in-process idiom) and MI-native token acquisition for a pinned UAMI.</role>

  <goal>IDataverseEnvironmentRegistryClient + its DefaultAzureCredential-backed implementation exist in Registry/. NullDataverseEnvironmentRegistryClient's consumers can DI-swap onto the real client (this task builds the client; task 122 performs H0.5's swap). Read + PATCH operations against a test/dev sprk_dataverseenvironment row succeed under the L2 UAMI's identity (post task 111's grant).</goal>

  <context>
    <background>DS-8 §1 confirms L2's registry read client and H13's Ready writer are today PURE PLACEHOLDERS (NullDataverseEnvironmentRegistryClient, no-op DataverseRegistrySetupStatusUpdater) -- greenfield either way per DS-2 §4 Level-3's note. DS-8's rollout plan step 3 specifies building this client MI-native from day one: 'raw HttpClient + DefaultAzureCredential(ManagedIdentityClientId), {adminEnvUrl}/.default scope -- same idiom as DataverseWebApiHealthProbe'.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Registry/IDataverseEnvironmentRegistryClient.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Registry/DataverseEnvironmentRegistryClient.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Registry/NullDataverseEnvironmentRegistryClient.cs (stays as the Null-Object fallback per ADR-032 pattern)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/DataverseEnvCreation/IDataverseHealthProbe.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Concurrency/CustomerRunGuardOptions.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="111" status="pending">The L2 UAMI must be a registered Dataverse App User with the scoped role before this client's calls will authorize</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec.md FR-38">L2's admin-env Dataverse credential model is Path X: L2 UAMI registered as a Dataverse Application User via DefaultAzureCredential pinned to the UAMI (DS-8). MUST NOT provision a new client-secret for L2. The Dataverse-ClientSecret KV secret itself MUST NOT be deleted (BFF still consumes it) -- only L2's dependency on it is removed.</constraint>
    <constraint source="design.md §9.6">Path X mechanics: L2 UAMI is registered as a Dataverse Application User on the ADMIN environment only, with a scoped custom security role ("Spaarke Provisioning Registry") -- NOT System Administrator. Registration is idempotent (find-by-applicationid, then check-then-add role association), matching the H10 DataverseWebApiAppUserCreator idiom (DS-8 Sec.4).</constraint>
    <constraint source="DS-8 §6 rollout step 3">Build C1.4 registry client MI-native from day one (raw HttpClient + DefaultAzureCredential(ManagedIdentityClientId), {adminEnvUrl}/.default scope) -- the two H13/H0.5 placeholders swap onto it (task 122, task 184), NOT this task.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-032">The NullDataverseEnvironmentRegistryClient stays as the Null-Object kill-switch fallback per the repo's existing P1/P2/P3 pattern -- this task ADDS the real implementation, it does not delete the Null-Object.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>C1.4 L2 Dataverse registry client</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/design.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/design-study-ds4-handler-audit.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/design-study-ds8-uami-dv-appuser-maturity.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-032-bff-nullobject-kill-switch.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="MI-native Dataverse Web API client" location="src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/DataverseEnvCreation/ (H5 health probe)">Raw HttpClient + DefaultAzureCredential idiom L2 already uses for H5/H10/H11/H12c -- this client follows the same shape pointed at the admin env instead of a customer env.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor + load">Emit RIGOR LEVEL (FULL). Read DS-8 §6 rollout plan in full plus the existing H5 health-probe client shape.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Interface">Author IDataverseEnvironmentRegistryClient: ReadByCustomerAsync(customerId, tenantId), UpdateSetupStatusAsync(environmentId, status, ...) matching the fields H13/H0.5 need.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Implementation">Author DataverseEnvironmentRegistryClient using HttpClient + DefaultAzureCredential(new DefaultAzureCredentialOptions{ManagedIdentityClientId=...}), token scope {adminEnvUrl}/.default, targeting sprk_dataverseenvironment via the standard Dataverse Web API $filter/PATCH idiom.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Register">Register in a Registry module (Scoped), config-bound to the admin env URL.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Tests">Unit tests against a fake HttpMessageHandler-free contract (per ADR-038 ban on HttpMessageHandler mocks) -- test the request-shape-building logic as pure functions where possible; integration seam test against dev spaarkedev1 (post task 111 grant) for a real read + PATCH round-trip.</step>
    <step order="5" name="Build + verify">dotnet build 0 errors; dotnet test green.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a live read/PATCH against spaarkedev1 under the UAMI's identity returns 403 despite task 111's grant appearing complete, STOP and escalate rather than widening the scoped role's privileges ad hoc — trace the exact prv* privilege the 403 names and add ONLY that privilege to the Grant-ControlPlaneIdentity.ps1-authored role definition (task 111), re-running that script rather than patching around the client.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">build/test</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Registry/IDataverseEnvironmentRegistryClient.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Registry/DataverseEnvironmentRegistryClient.cs</output>
    <output type="test">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Tests/Registry/DataverseEnvironmentRegistryClientTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">IDataverseEnvironmentRegistryClient + implementation build with 0 errors.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">grep 'ClientSecretCredential' in DataverseEnvironmentRegistryClient.cs returns 0 matches (Path X only -- no new secret credential).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Integration seam test: a read against a known dev sprk_dataverseenvironment row (or a canary row created for the test) succeeds under the L2 UAMI's identity.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Integration seam test: a PATCH to sprk_setupstatus on the same canary row succeeds and a subsequent read reflects the new value.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">dotnet build exits 0; dotnet test exits 0.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Justification (CLAUDE.md §11): Existing -- NullDataverseEnvironmentRegistryClient is a placeholder that always returns null (FR-02 re-consent semantics inert per DS-4). Extension -- cannot extend a Null-Object into a real client; a genuine implementation is required, but it follows the SAME MI-native idiom H5/H10/H11/H12c already prove works. Cost-of-doing-nothing -- H0.5's re-consent branch stays permanently inert (task 122 has nothing to swap onto), and H13's Ready-writer transition (task 184, the acceptance-target transition itself) stays a logged no-op.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
  </execution>
</task>
